{"name":"Bell Heather","hex":"#a475b1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bell heather","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A species of heather, native to western and central Europe, Erica cinerea; heather-bell"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bell_heather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Erica cinerea","blocks":[{"text":"Erica cinerea, the bell heather, is a species of flowering plant in the heath family Ericaceae, native to western and central Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Bell_Heather_-_geograph.org.uk_-_493968.jpg/330px-Bell_Heather_-_geograph.org.uk_-_493968.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erica_cinerea","wikidata":"Q1543735"},{"title":"Bell","blocks":[{"text":"A bell is a directly struck idiophone percussion instrument. Most bells have the shape of a hollow cup that—when struck—vibrates in a single strong strike tone, with its sides forming an efficient resonator. The strike may be made by an internal \"clapper\" or \"uvula\", an external hammer, or—in small bells—by a small loose sphere enclosed within the body of the bell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Parts_of_a_Bell.svg/330px-Parts_of_a_Bell.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell","wikidata":"Q101401"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg/500px-13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg/1280px-13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/13th-12th